1
00:00:01,450 --> 00:00:04,700
Narrator: PinPatch. A little play about learning from failure.

2
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:13,757
Narrator: Meet Robo. A small, seven billion parameter robot, with a big job.

3
00:00:14,407 --> 00:00:17,054
Robo: Today's task: measure the temperature of the water!

4
00:00:17,604 --> 00:00:21,621
Robo: Go to the kitchen. Pick up the water. Focus on... the flower pot?

5
00:00:23,271 --> 00:00:26,127
Narrator: One wrong step, and the whole episode fails.

6
00:00:26,677 --> 00:00:28,210
Robo: Oh no. What went wrong?

7
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:34,748
Professor LLM: Ahem! Let me diagnose you, young robot.

8
00:00:35,498 --> 00:00:37,936
Professor LLM: Clearly, you should... be more careful!

9
00:00:39,186 --> 00:00:42,553
Robo: But... which step? Maybe step four? Or step one?

10
00:00:44,203 --> 00:00:49,404
Narrator: Asked to judge its own failure, a small model just guesses. No better than random.

11
00:00:52,854 --> 00:00:56,918
Detective Pin: Allow me. I don't ask for opinions. I read the evidence.

12
00:00:57,568 --> 00:01:02,909
Narrator: Detective Pin reads Robo's hidden state, trained only on whether episodes succeed or fail.

13
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:06,150
Detective Pin: Here. Step three. The focus.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,556
Dr. Patch: A small patch should do it.

15
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:15,026
Dr. Patch: Now, let's rehearse it once more.

16
00:01:16,876 --> 00:01:20,545
Dr. Patch: It works, and nothing else broke. Into the library it goes!

17
00:01:22,195 --> 00:01:25,121
Narrator: No lessons written. Only fixes that work.

18
00:01:28,371 --> 00:01:31,064
Robo: Kitchen. Water. Which cup, Professor?

19
00:01:31,514 --> 00:01:32,490
Professor LLM: The glass one!

20
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:36,210
The Guard: Stop right there. Not the flower pot.

21
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,043
Robo: Thanks! Reading the thermometer... done!

22
00:01:40,493 --> 00:01:46,066
Narrator: Most steps need no LLM at all, and a guard reading the same hidden state blocks fatal moves.

23
00:01:49,316 --> 00:01:53,426
Narrator: Thank you for watching our little play. Now, the real results.

24
00:01:58,476 --> 00:02:10,387
Narrator: On four AgentGym environments, with the same seven billion parameter model, PinPatch outperforms thirteen prompting agents, and a model fine-tuned on eight thousand six hundred expert trajectories.

25
00:02:11,837 --> 00:02:17,526
Narrator: It needs just four point eight LLM calls per episode. About a quarter of the fine-tuned model.

26
00:02:18,776 --> 00:02:27,786
Narrator: When the LLM diagnoses its own failures, it is no better than random. PinPatch's outcome-supervised credit finds the fix in fewer tries.

27
00:02:29,036 --> 00:02:33,053
Narrator: And it holds across five model families, with nothing retuned.

28
00:02:36,903 --> 00:02:42,522
Narrator: PinPatch. Learning from failure, without self-diagnosis. The code is on GitHub.

